==English==
{{wikipedia|wrong (disambiguation)|wrong}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|wrong}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wrang||wrong, twisted, uneven}}, from {{der|en|non|rangr}}, {{m|non|*vrangr||crooked, wrong}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*wrangaz||crooked, twisted, turned awry}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*werḱ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*wrengʰ-||to twist, weave, tie together}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*wer-||to turn, bend}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|wrang||wrong}}, {{cog|da|vrang||wrong, crooked}}, {{cog|sv|vrång||perverse, distorted}}, {{cog|is|rangur||wrong}}, {{cog|nn|rang||wrong}}, {{cog|nl|wrang||bitter, sour}} and the first element in the mythic {{cog|ofs|-}} city of {{m|ofs|Rungholt||crooked wood}}. More at [[wring]].

